  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Technology obligated $492M in FY2026 to date across 125 awards, with an average award size of $3.9M. Obligations are up 13.3% year over year. Current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $290M, followed by the Department of Defense with $188M. The General Services Administration, Department of Health and Human Services, Environmental Protection Agency, and Department of Homeland Security account for smaller shares at $8.5M, $3.5M, $1.6M, and $102K respectively. Engineering Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) are the top NAICS markets at $197M and $192M. Facilities Support Services represents $97M. Historical obligations show higher totals in prior years, with FY21 and FY22 at $1.2B each, FY23 at $947M, FY24 at $600M, and FY25 at $434M. This snapshot shows where Amentum Technology is concentrated in buyers and markets through the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Amentum Technology's largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $290M to Amentum Technology in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $188M. The General Services Administration, Department of Health and Human Services, Environmental Protection Agency, and Department of Homeland Security obligated $8.5M, $3.5M, $1.6M, and $102K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Amentum Technology's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market at $197M, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $192M. Facilities Support Services accounts for $97M. The NAICS list also includes Landscape Architectural Services at $145K and Computer Systems Design Services at -$3.5M."
      }
    ]
